1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,385
Nvidia, the chip maker at the heart of the AI boom,

2
00:00:03,385 --> 00:00:06,937
has lost almost half its value in about seven weeks.

3
00:00:06,937 --> 00:00:09,818
On Friday alone, it fell 14%.

4
00:00:09,818 --> 00:00:13,906
The Nasdaq had its worst week since March 2020, and

5
00:00:13,906 --> 00:00:18,195
the S&P 500 and the Dow slipped into a correction.

6
00:00:18,195 --> 00:00:19,402
So what happened?

7
00:00:19,402 --> 00:00:21,211
Is the AI bubble bursting?

8
00:00:21,211 --> 00:00:24,160
And what does it mean for the future of AI?

9
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:25,800
Let's break it down.

10
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,637
In early October, Nvidia closed at a record of about

11
00:00:29,637 --> 00:00:34,954
$239 a share, worth close to $6 trillion.

12
00:00:34,954 --> 00:00:39,948
By Friday's close, it was down to about $125.

13
00:00:39,948 --> 00:00:42,866
That's a fall of around 47%.

14
00:00:42,866 --> 00:00:47,470
Last week alone, it dropped 23%, its worst week since

15
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:49,780
October 2008.

16
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:51,663
Reason one is money.

17
00:00:51,663 --> 00:00:55,438
Big tech companies are spending hundreds of billions

18
00:00:55,438 --> 00:00:58,145
of dollars on chips and data centres.

19
00:00:58,145 --> 00:01:01,921
Investors are now asking a simple question: how fast

20
00:01:01,921 --> 00:01:04,842
will all that spending turn into profit?

21
00:01:04,842 --> 00:01:08,475
Nvidia's latest results beat expectations, but the

22
00:01:08,475 --> 00:01:10,042
doubt didn't go away.

23
00:01:10,042 --> 00:01:13,676
When a stock is priced for perfection, doubt alone

24
00:01:13,676 --> 00:01:15,187
can push it down.

25
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,301
Reason two is politics.

26
00:01:17,301 --> 00:01:21,555
After the US midterm elections on 3 November, investors

27
00:01:21,555 --> 00:01:25,170
began to worry about tighter rules for AI and more

28
00:01:25,170 --> 00:01:27,864
local opposition to new data centres.

29
00:01:27,864 --> 00:01:29,849
Reason three is leadership.

30
00:01:29,849 --> 00:01:34,244
On 12 November, Nvidia's co-founder and chief executive,

31
00:01:34,244 --> 00:01:37,718
Jensen Huang, resigned after 33 years.

32
00:01:37,718 --> 00:01:41,475
Finance chief Colette Kress is now interim CEO while

33
00:01:41,475 --> 00:01:44,540
the board searches for a permanent one.

34
00:01:45,033 --> 00:01:46,970
Reason four is interest rates.

35
00:01:46,970 --> 00:01:50,518
Markets now expect the Federal Reserve to raise rates

36
00:01:50,518 --> 00:01:51,372
in December.

37
00:01:51,372 --> 00:01:54,723
Higher rates make future profits worth less today.

38
00:01:54,723 --> 00:01:58,140
That hits fast-growing tech stocks hardest, because

39
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:01,622
so much of their value depends on profits many years

40
00:02:01,622 --> 00:02:02,513
from now.

41
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,710
Here's the maths of a crash.

42
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:09,141
If you had put $1,000 into Nvidia at its October record,

43
00:02:09,141 --> 00:02:13,260
it would now be worth about $525.

44
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:17,067
To get back to 1,000, the stock now has to rise about

45
00:02:17,067 --> 00:02:18,315
91%.

46
00:02:18,315 --> 00:02:23,308
In general, a 50% fall needs a 100% gain just to break

47
00:02:23,308 --> 00:02:23,920
even.

48
00:02:24,433 --> 00:02:26,507
So, is the AI bubble bursting?

49
00:02:26,507 --> 00:02:30,365
Nobody knows for sure, but history offers two lessons.

50
00:02:30,365 --> 00:02:34,433
After the dot-com bubble in 2000, the Nasdaq fell

51
00:02:34,433 --> 00:02:38,991
nearly 80%, yet the internet kept growing and changed

52
00:02:38,991 --> 00:02:39,763
the world.

53
00:02:39,763 --> 00:02:44,322
Nvidia itself fell about two-thirds in 2022, before

54
00:02:44,322 --> 00:02:46,706
AI demand sent it to new records.

55
00:02:46,706 --> 00:02:50,793
Share prices and technology can move very differently.

56
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:54,857
What to watch next: how much big tech plans to spend

57
00:02:54,857 --> 00:02:58,514
on AI next year, the Fed's decision in December, new

58
00:02:58,514 --> 00:03:02,309
rules on AI and data centres, and who becomes Nvidia's

59
00:03:02,309 --> 00:03:02,999
next CEO.

60
00:03:02,999 --> 00:03:06,588
This video is for education, not investment advice.

61
